","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T16:03:23-08:00","id":19934,"title":"","content":"Whatever...I am trying to diet and this holiday is not conductive to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T18:22:10-08:00","id":20003,"title":"","content":"I know it's easy to be cynical about this holiday--&quot;Gosh, I'm so thankful a bunch of Christian zealots too tight-assed for even the British to tolerate 'found' a land indigenous people were already living on and began a genocidal crusade that ensconced the nation as an imperial power who now treats this holiday as an excuse for gluttony and a prelude to commercialism of the very religion the nation was born from!&quot;--but screw that noise. It's stupid and reflexive and useless. Let this be a time to be thankful for what life has given us and what we can enjoy, and I'm thankful I have my family, I have my friends (that includes you guys), I have enough food to eat and more than enough food to eat, I have warmth and shelter and clothing. I have a magic book under my fingers that can talk to anyone on the planet and receive their thoughts in return, and possesses access to all human knowledge ever recorded throughout history. I am grateful for my life, mostly because of the people I've met here, and I hope some small sliver or my gratitude is warming to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:09:07-08:00","id":20017,"title":"","content":"I think most are familiar enough of history to realize the &quot;Thanksgiving&quot; myth for what it is, but can appreciate and enjoy the tradition that it has become.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T19:22:20-08:00","id":20024,"title":"","content":"Happy Turkey Day everyone, always look forward to the leftovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1393-bent-twig","name":"Bent Twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1393_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T20:02:32-08:00","id":20035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/19802-happy-thanksgiving?p=20003#post20003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it's easy to be cynical about this holiday--&quot;Gosh, I'm so thankful a bunch of Christian zealots too tight-assed for even the British to tolerate 'found' a land indigenous people were already living on and began a genocidal crusade that ensconced the nation as an imperial power who now treats this holiday as an excuse for gluttony and a prelude to commercialism of the very religion the nation was born from!&quot;--but screw that noise. It's stupid and reflexive and useless. Let this be a time to be thankful for what life has given us and what we can enjoy, and I'm thankful I have my family, I have my friends (that includes you guys), I have enough food to eat and more than enough food to eat, I have warmth and shelter and clothing. I have a magic book under my fingers that can talk to anyone on the planet and receive their thoughts in return, and possesses access to all human knowledge ever recorded throughout history. I am grateful for my life, mostly because of the people I've met here, and I hope some small sliver or my gratitude is warming to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I Guess? <br /> <br /> To me it's more of a combination of thanks for the survival of the christian zealots against very great odds (with the help of the natives who took some pity on them) and your bog standard Harvest Festival, which is seen the world over. Sure there are a lot of dark overtones with the settlers. On both sides. I mean sure the original colonies survived... they just frequently lost the majority of the population every winter and resorted to cannibalism to survive at times. <br /> <br /> But it's also a harvest celebration. Gather villagers, for we have wood to last the winter, we have grain stocks to last to summer, and we have slaughtered the herds so eat what you will of this food while it is fresh, because what we can't preserve in the next few days will be gone. Be fat and joyful, and pray we survive!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-28T20:08:14-08:00","id":20039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/19802-happy-thanksgiving?p=20035#post20035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I Guess?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, like I said, it's stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","cust